  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(335.52pt, 542.16pt, "]. The most conventional methodology utilizes ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 554.04pt, "pixelated heating elements integrated with direct wire addressing circuits [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#69bd45"))
  #line-at(385.32pt, 554.04pt, "16")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(395.28pt, 554.04pt, "]. This approach can in principle ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 566.04pt, "generate complex thermal patterns, but has limited scalability. Recently, advanced materials such as multi-")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 577.92pt, "layer carbon-fiber-reinforced polymers, carbon nanotubes (CNTs) [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#69bd45"))
  #line-at(346.56pt, 577.92pt, "17")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(355.68pt, 577.92pt, ", ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#69bd45"))
  #line-at(360.24pt, 577.92pt, "18")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(370.32pt, 577.92pt, "], Fe/Ni/Co alloy (Invar) [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#69bd45"))
  #line-at(483.12pt, 577.92pt, "19")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(492.96pt, 577.92pt, "] have also ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 589.8pt, "been incorporated in heater designs, thereby broadening potential applications. Still, demonstrations have been ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 601.8pt, "limited to directly-wired single heating elements [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#69bd45"))
  #line-at(275.28pt, 601.8pt, "20")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(286.92pt, 601.8pt, "] or to small array sizes [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#69bd45"))
  #line-at(394.32pt, 601.8pt, "21")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(404.16pt, 601.8pt, "]. The scale-up to larger multi-")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 613.68pt, "pixel arrays presents a major challenge, demanding uniform electrical characteristics of the material across all ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 625.68pt, "the elements of an array [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#69bd45"))
  #line-at(169.08pt, 625.68pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(174.6pt, 625.68pt, ", ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#69bd45"))
  #line-at(178.68pt, 625.68pt, "4")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(184.32pt, 625.68pt, ", ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#69bd45"))
  #line-at(188.28pt, 625.68pt, "22")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(199.32pt, 625.68pt, "], as well as a scalable architecture.")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 643.8pt, "Large numbers of fine, closely spaced heating elements promise the generation of sophisticated heat patterns and ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 655.68pt, "potentially steep thermal gradients. However, as the feature size decreases it becomes progressively more difficult ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 667.68pt, "to generate sufficient heat, since the resistance drops with shorter conductor lines, and a significant difference in ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 679.56pt, "the impedance of the microheater cell and the interconnected input power lines is needed. Moreover, it becomes ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 691.44pt, "challenging to address large arrays, as wiring large number of heaters becomes challenging. For instance, wiring ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 703.44pt, "each element separately becomes impractical. Herein, we show how high-speed row/column addressing can be ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 715.32pt, "used to overcome these challenges and how this enables the selective activation of any individual elements within ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 727.32pt, "the array. We thereby demonstrate the fabrication, control and operation of, what to the best of our knowledge ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 739.2pt, "is the largest microheater array to date.")
]

