  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(234pt, 586.68pt, "32 heater array are connected to a custom-built digitally controlled ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 599.64pt, "electronics board to enable individual addressing of the microheater elements. The primary function of the ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 610.68pt, "board is to control the high voltage (V")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(229.32pt, 611.64pt, "DD")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(239.64pt, 610.68pt, ") channel switch with a low voltage digital signal (V")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(473.52pt, 611.64pt, "LL")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#231f20"))
  #line-at(481.32pt, 610.68pt, "). The high-")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 622.56pt, "voltage switch opens or closes the circuit to generate the target pattern. The switch is normally open and ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 634.44pt, "requires a 5-bit code for switching operation which is controlled by a microcontroller (Arduino Mega 2560). ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 646.44pt, "The row electrodes are connected to the output terminal of a high voltage amplifier (WMA-300, Falco Systems ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 658.32pt, "GmbH) and the column electrodes are connected to ground. The following electronics components are used in ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 670.2pt, "the construction of the board: Demultiplexer - CD74HC4067M (Texas Instruments), Shift-Register - SNLS674 ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 682.2pt, "(Texas Instruments), and High Voltage Channel Switch - TMUX9616 (Texas Instruments). LPC 6/3-ST-7.62 ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 694.08pt, "PCB connectors (Phoenix Contact) are soldered on the board for the DC and HV voltage supply. The thermal ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 706.08pt, "pattern is generated by sequentially switching ON the microheater pixels where the 5-bit code is loaded through ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 717.96pt, "external CLK pulses. The pixels are heated for a fixed duration based on the temperature requirements of the ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 729.96pt, "output. The high voltage signal profile remains unchanged, but the switches are controlled via the 5-bit input ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 741.84pt, "code and the CLK pulses.")
]

